            <div xml:id="d405-a1">

                <pb facs="0737" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg637"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    284.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract from Le Moniteur, June 17,
                    1880.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The government desires to announce that international law accords to it the
                    absolute right to expel Irom our territory foreigners who seek to trouble public
                    order.</p>
                <p>The government announces also, that according to universal law of nations,
                    consuls, and consular agents, are subject to local jurisdiction, especially when
                    engaged in commerce, and that diplomatic immunities only affect public ministers
                    and the personnel of their legations.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
